%% leads, never here). Likewise for pages and years: a field that could not
%% be resolved is omitted and the `note` says so.
%%
%% EVERY entry carries a mandatory `note` of the form
%%     note = {evidence: <label>; provenance: <one sentence>}
%% followed, where needed, by an explicit flag of what is still unresolved.
%%
%% EVIDENCE LABELS
%%   METADATA_VERIFIED            instruction-file record (identity checked
%%                                by the instruction file's own author)
%%   METADATA_VERIFIED(index)     title/authors/journal corroborated across
%%                                >=2 independently phrased search queries,
%%                                and/or a DOI-bearing publisher URL seen
%%   METADATA_VERIFIED(index, single)   one query only -- weaker
%%   +ABSTRACT(index)             abstract-level text from the search
%%                                summariser; WEAKER than SECTION_READ
%%   SECTION_READ                 the passage was actually read (GitHub
%%                                READMEs; plus [P04] per the instruction file)
%%   PROJECT_INPUT                asserted by the instruction file
%%   UNVERIFIED                   provenance unresolved, or the claim rests
%%                                on a single summariser sentence
%%
%% STRUCTURE
%%   Part 1  Books and book chapters (instruction file [B01]-[B15], [C01]-[C03])
%%   Part 2  Papers recorded by the instruction file ([P01]-[P07])
%%   Part 3  Software records from the instruction file ([S01]-[S02])
%%   Part 4  Records added by B_literature.md ([P08]-[P51], [PAT01], and
%%           software actually read)
%%   Part 5  %% ===== UNVERIFIED CANDIDATES (do not cite without checking) =====
